module Core

# ============================================================================
# The 128-bit fast phases of lgamma and tgamma of B128, for the D128 transcendentals (D128Fast.rf). B128.lgamma
# and tgamma_unchecked themselves are Tessera's, through Ingrid.
# ============================================================================
# Below 24, x = 2 + z + n with |z| <= 1/2: lgamma(2 + z) = z Q(z) from its series in zeta values, and the
# factors x - 1 .. x - n (or the divisions x, x (1 + x) below 3/2) are exact, so lgamma adds ln of their
# product and tgamma multiplies e^(z Q) by it. From 24 on, Stirling's series with the sum in u = 24/x;
# for tgamma the exponent (x - 1/2) ln x - x + ln(2 pi)/2 + sum reaches 11356, so it is formed in fixed
# point from the whole 192-bit CORE-MATH logarithm, as in pow. Each result keeps a proven error bound
# (B128Fx).

# lgamma(2 + z) / z around the centres c = i/32 (i = -16 .. 16): Q(c + t) = sum_k q_k t^k for |t| <= 1/64,
# 19 coefficients per centre (the rest below 0.05 units), in units of 2^-126. They come from the Taylor
# coefficients of lgamma at 2 + c, psi^(k-1)(2 + c) / k!, through c q_k + q_(k-1) = l_k.
